      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-31T15:07:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "just have a normal USB driver be bound to your device, it will be notified when a USB device is found that matches what you are looking for.\n\nOr use the in-kernel USB notifier that notifies you already of all USB devices being added or removed in the system.  No Android-specific hook should be needed at all here.",
      "revId": "56903ea6798ab722bdadc8bf3112886bb6f70bce",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d623fac9_70e04e79",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125653
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-31T15:08:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Also, you had a year to get your dwc3 changes upstream, based on the previous hook.  What happened to them that still requires this one?",
      "revId": "56903ea6798ab722bdadc8bf3112886bb6f70bce",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "854d52af_e651abb5",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1943840
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-06-01T01:42:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Dear Greg,\nThere are two controller: dwc3 3.1/2.0 controller and SPRD 2.0 controller in UNISOC platform.\nWe use dwc3 controller by default. SPRD 2.0 controller is only used for audio offload feature.\nWe need this hook to do:\n1, prevent the headset devices be registered into system with dwc3 controller\n2, to notify dwc3 controller exit\n3, to start SPRD 2.0 controller, then enumerate the USB headset device again.\n\nIt not common feature, no changes in dwc3 just exit, but we really need this hook to realize UNISOC‘s feature.",
      "parentUuid": "d623fac9_70e04e79",
      "revId": "56903ea6798ab722bdadc8bf3112886bb6f70bce",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7753d65d_baecf3e1",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125653
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-06-01T06:32:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is a \"common\" feature because this is what your hardware does, and is how it works, so please submit the \"real\" change that is required upstream and we can discuss it there and then add it here, without any need for a hook.",
      "parentUuid": "854d52af_e651abb5",
      "revId": "56903ea6798ab722bdadc8bf3112886bb6f70bce",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "592499f4_82cbacab",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1943840
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-06-01T09:20:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Dear Greg,\nNormally it should not required. It\u0027s really UNISOC ASIC design drawback. In UNISOC, Synopsys controller + PHY doesn\u0027t support USB audio offload feature. It\u0027s need to switch to MUSB controller when USB headset detected.\n\nThe realization is bad, these codes should not be upstreamed to destroy the Linux elegant style. But for UNISOC， we cannot change the design now, it\u0027s the efficiency way to resolve design issue.",
      "parentUuid": "7753d65d_baecf3e1",
      "revId": "56903ea6798ab722bdadc8bf3112886bb6f70bce",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ec60891e_99b347a2",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125653
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-06-01T11:23:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You can not continue to add \"unelegant\" hooks like this to the Android kernel for forever.  Please submit your changes properly upstream first, that\u0027s always a requirement for hooks, they are never guaranteed to be accepted in the future.",
      "parentUuid": "592499f4_82cbacab",
      "revId": "56903ea6798ab722bdadc8bf3112886bb6f70bce",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
